  "description": "The proposed works involve the replacement of the existing single-glazed timber sash windows with new double-glazed timber sash windows on the front and side elevations of the property.\n\nThe new windows will be identical in design and appearance to the originals, with matching timber frames, sash proportions, glazing bar patterns, and opening mechanisms.\n\nThe only material change is the use of slimline double glazing in place of single glazing. This will deliver significantly improved thermal efficiency and reduce energy loss, while maintaining the building’s historic character. The units will use clear glass only, and all external timber components will be finished in heritage-style microporous paint.\n\nThe property lies within a designated conservation area and is subject to an Article 4 Direction, and great care has been taken to ensure the proposed works are in keeping with the existing architectural detail and do not harm the character or appearance of the building or the wider street scene.\n\nThere is no change of use proposed as part of this application.",
